{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3073","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3073","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3073\",\"parent_revision\":\"e9fdbf32214ccc5891e2043603294a50d1e18776\",\"root_revision\":\"b0782ca4c7fe6589d452fc93488a54a62c68e415135386e618d4382b8e746200\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Decision Needed\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRecorded as open question 2 in `docs/agent-markdown-consumption-contract.md`, with no backlog\\ntracking until now.\\n\\nR6 requires the section table of contents and the artifact inventory to arrive in one response.\\nR2 requires that a table of contents exceeding budget paginates rather than drops content. When\\nboth the table of contents and the artifact inventory are individually large enough to threaten\\nthe budget on their own, undecided:\\n\\n- Page them together as one combined paginated sequence, or\\n- Page each independently (two separate page cursors/identifiers in the same response)\\n</div>\\n\\n## Why This Blocks Work\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n#3061 (\\\"return sections and artifacts as one inventory\\\") implements R6's combined response\\nshape. Its acceptance criteria do not currently address the both-oversized case \u2014 this decision\\nmust land before #3061 can claim R2 compliance for that case, not after.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Resolution\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nUpdate `docs/agent-markdown-consumption-contract.md`'s open-questions section to remove item 2\\nonce decided, and record the chosen composition directly in the contract as a normative\\nrequirement (likely amending R6 or R2's \\\"Required flow\\\" diagram).\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"52c20ca019667c22145ba4d10b2f6c994d9c572931d3bd4366596393ee025181\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABP8480w\"}"}